The correct answer is __**Instant messaging**__.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• **Instant messaging** is a form of real-time communication between two or more users over a network.

• This service allows users to create a private chat room where they can communicate instantly.

• Instant messaging applications include features such as text messaging, file sharing, and sometimes voice and video calling.

• Popular instant messaging platforms include WhatsApp, Facebook Messenger, WeChat, and Slack.

• Instant messaging can be used for both personal and professional communication, making it a versatile tool for various purposes.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• Instant messaging provides the advantage of quick and direct communication, which can enhance productivity and connectivity.

• Many instant messaging applications offer end-to-end encryption to ensure the security and privacy of the conversations.

• Instant messaging can be integrated with other tools and services, such as email and cloud storage, for a seamless user experience.

• The concept of instant messaging dates back to the early days of the internet, with early services like ICQ and AOL Instant Messenger (AIM) paving the way for modern applications.

